      "writtenOn": "2026-07-27T10:48:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since ftdi_mdio.cpp and mdio.cpp are currently only used by meta/ventura2.cpp, would it make sense to gate them behind a meson feature option? Currently, util_srcs links them into every platform\u0027s binary (intel \u0026 nvidia), and it would be great if non-meta platforms could opt out.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 44,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "4c83606783fc49ef9524bbb3de235747abe4feba",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e32ffc4b_71dbd30f",
        "filename": "meson.build",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002520
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-28T13:28:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for pointing that out. I actually missed that these sources were being built into every platform binary. I added an MDIO Meson feature option and now gate ftdi_mdio.cpp and mdio.cpp behind it. Ventura2 enables this feature through PACKAGECONFIG, while other platforms can build without the MDIO sources and dependencies.\n\n\n@amithash@meta.com @jamesatha@meta.com Could you please help review this change?",
      "parentUuid": "2da8857a_2ea95495",
